{##
 # Standardised Test
 #
 # @param array     externalUser
 # @param int|null  year
 # @param array     STARTable
 # @param array     STARStanine
 #}
{% include '@templates/Avatar.twig' %}

{% include '@templates/Navigation.twig' with {
    elements: navigation
} %}

{% include '@templates/Navigation.twig' with {
    elements: subnavigation
} %}

<div class="achievement-report standardised-test">
    <div class="row">
        <div class="small-12 columns">
            {% include '@standardisedTest/STAR/Table/Table.twig' with {
                data: STARTable.data
            } %}
        </div>
    </div>

    {% include '@standardisedTest/STAR/Stanine/Navigation.twig' with {
        elements: STARStanineNavigation
    } %}

    {% if STARStanine.visible %}
        <div class="small-12 columns">
            {% include '@standardisedTest/Stanine/Graph.twig' with {
                identifier: 'STARStanine',
                title: STARStanine.data.graph.title,
                yAxis: STARStanine.data.graph.y,
                series: STARStanine.data.series
            } %}
        </div>
    {% endif %}

    <div class="row">
        <div class="small-12 island">
            <section class="content">
                <p>
                    <strong>STAR Test:</strong> There are four parts to the STAR Test which assess different reading
                    skills including Word Recognition, Sentence Comprehension, Paragraph Comprehension, and Vocabulary
                    Range. PAT Tests: Progressive Achievement Tests are a series of standardised tests developed
                    specifically for New Zealand Schools. There are four different tests: Reading Comprehension, Reading
                    Vocabulary, Listening Comprehension, and Mathematics.
                </p>

                <p>
                    <strong>Stanines:</strong> Each set of year level results is depicted as a graph showing the
                    percentage of students gaining stanine 1 to 9 on a national level compared to Diocesan Junior
                    School. There is no notion of a pass or fail in these scores. They merely represent the ability of
                    the student in comparison to other students of the same age in New Zealand at that point in time.
                </p>

                <p>
                    Your daughter's results are indicated by the star.
                </p>
            </section>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
